.TH GETCWD 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
getcwd \- obtain the current working directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B char* getcwd(char* buffer, size_t size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes the absolute directory path and its NUL terminator into buffer.  With
NULL buffer, allocates size bytes, or automatically sizes the allocation when
size is zero.  Free the returned allocation with free.
This implementation uses the Linux getcwd syscall and does not provide GNU
libc's fallback for paths exceeding the kernel syscall's length limit.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the buffer, or NULL with errno set.  An unreachable directory is
reported as ENOENT.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getcwd (3),
.BR getcwd (2)
